  data: {
    LLM: "Use the ascending order to your advantage. If an opponent reveals a 10 at Position 4 (out of 6), you know that Positions 1-3 MUST be lower than 10, and Positions 5-6 MUST be higher than 10.\n\nThe Partner Signal: When your partner shows you a card, they are often showing you a 'boundary' card (like a 6 or 7). Use this to deduce their other cards and narrow down the possibilities for the opponents.\n\nElimination Logic: If you know your team has both Aces, and no opponent has revealed an Ace yet, you can 'waste' a guess on an opponent's first position to see if they reveal a 2 or 3. Even an incorrect guess on your part provides information to your partner.",
    Player: "Use the ascending order to your advantage. If an opponent reveals a 10 at Position 4 (out of 6), you know that Positions 1-3 MUST be lower than 10, and Positions 5-6 MUST be higher than 10.\n\nThe Partner Signal: When your partner shows you a card, they are often showing you a 'boundary' card (like a 6 or 7). Use this to deduce their other cards and narrow down the possibilities for the opponents.\n\nElimination Logic: If you know your team has both Aces, and no opponent has revealed an Ace yet, you can 'waste' a guess on an opponent's first position to see if they reveal a 2 or 3. Even an incorrect guess on your part provides information to your partner.",
